<title>UK: Tex in six mln stg deal with Philipino firm.</title>
<headline>Tex in six mln stg deal with Philipino firm.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>British building engineering group Tex Holdings Plc said on Wednesday that it had signed a six million stg contract with Laguna Property Holdings Inc, a wholly owned division of Ayala Land of Manila, Philippines.</p>
<p>According to the contract, Tex, through a newly formed subsidiary of Tex Industrialised Construction Systems Ltd, would supply Laguna specialised engineering plant and equipment to make concrete building panels in the Philippines.</p>
<p>The contract would be executed until June 1998, Tex said in a statement.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
